---
import SceneFrame from './SceneFrame.astro';

const code = `worker := varmq.NewErrWorker(process, "mailer")`;
---

<SceneFrame scene="errors" title="Where a failure goes" code={code} hint="// add a job: the call it makes and what it returns show here">
	<Fragment slot="stats">
		<div><dt>Submitted</dt><dd data-stat="submitted">0</dd></div>
		<div><dt>Completed</dt><dd data-stat="completed">0</dd></div>
		<div><dt>Successful</dt><dd data-stat="successful">0</dd></div>
		<div><dt>Failed</dt><dd data-stat="failed">0</dd></div>
	</Fragment>

	<div class="gb-boxes">
		<section class="gb-box" aria-labelledby="gb-err-h1">
			<p class="gb-label" id="gb-err-h1">Job handle <b data-handle-name>Err()</b></p>
			<ul class="gb-list" data-handles></ul>
		</section>
		<section class="gb-box" aria-labelledby="gb-err-h2">
			<p class="gb-label" id="gb-err-h2">Errs() channel <b>room for 1</b></p>
			<p class="gb-slot" data-slot>empty</p>
			<p class="gb-drops" data-drops>dropped: 0</p>
			<p class="gb-note-line" data-reader-note>Nothing reads the channel.</p>
		</section>
		<section class="gb-box" aria-labelledby="gb-err-h3">
			<p class="gb-label" id="gb-err-h3">WithErrHandler <b>every failure</b></p>
			<ul class="gb-list" data-handler></ul>
		</section>
	</div>

	<Fragment slot="controls">
		<div class="gb-seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Worker type" data-type>
			<button type="button" class="gb-btn" role="radio" aria-checked="false" tabindex="-1" data-value="plain">NewWorker</button>
			<button type="button" class="gb-btn" role="radio" aria-checked="true" tabindex="0" data-value="err">NewErrWorker</button>
			<button type="button" class="gb-btn" role="radio" aria-checked="false" tabindex="-1" data-value="result">NewResultWorker</button>
		</div>
		<div class="gb-seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="What the function does" data-outcome>
			<button type="button" class="gb-btn" role="radio" aria-checked="false" tabindex="-1" data-value="ok">returns</button>
			<button type="button" class="gb-btn" role="radio" aria-checked="true" tabindex="0" data-value="error">fails</button>
			<button type="button" class="gb-btn" role="radio" aria-checked="false" tabindex="-1" data-value="panic">panics</button>
		</div>
		<button type="button" class="gb-btn gb-btn--primary" data-act="add">Add job</button>
		<button type="button" class="gb-btn" data-act="add3">Add 3 jobs</button>
		<button type="button" class="gb-btn" data-act="read">Read Errs()</button>
		<button type="button" class="gb-btn" data-act="reader" aria-pressed="false">Reader goroutine: off</button>
	</Fragment>

	<Fragment slot="alt">
		A simulation of a worker named mailer with a limit of 2. Pick a worker type and what its function does, then add
		jobs. A failure is reported in up to three places. The job handle of an error or result worker gets the error. A
		plain worker has no handle. The <code>Errs()</code> channel has room for one error, so when it is full the next
		error is dropped and counted. The error handler runs for every failure, including the dropped ones. A result
		worker returns the zero result when the function fails, even if the function also returned a value. The counters
		at the top are the four counters of <code>Metrics()</code>.
	</Fragment>
</SceneFrame>

<script>
	import './errors.ts';
</script>
